// =============================================================================
// LETTER OF COLLABORATION — NSF 26-506 requires a MINIMUM OF THREE and a
// MAXIMUM OF FIVE. Two pages maximum each.
//
// This is one of the biggest deviations from the PAPPG in this solicitation.
// The PAPPG's default is a single terse sentence of intent with no
// endorsement. PESOSE overrides that completely:
//
//   * Letters need NOT conform to the standard PAPPG format.
//   * Writers must be CURRENT users or contributors of the open-source
//     product who are NOT directly related to the proposing team. Someone on
//     your team, or at the lead organization, does not count.
//   * Each letter must describe how they HAVE contributed and how they WILL
//     CONTINUE to contribute to the proposed ecosystem.
//   * Each must state: writer's name, current affiliation (institution or
//     place of employment), and relationship to the proposing team.
//   * If the ecosystem will depend on facilities infrastructure provided by
//     any organization AFTER the award ends, include one additional letter
//     describing the extent and term of that provision.
//
// PRACTICAL NOTE: these have the longest lead time of anything in the
// package, because they depend on other people's calendars. Request them
// first. Every writer must also appear in 07-personnel-list/.
//
// Copy per letter: loc-01.typ, loc-02.typ, ... Collaborators will usually
// send you a PDF on their own letterhead, which is fine and often better —
// this template is for when someone asks you to draft something they can
// edit.
// =============================================================================

